244 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 86 0 R
/E (For the button band sts are picked up along the front edges and back neck cast on edge with a 3 mm / US 2.5 circular needle. The button band is worked in double knitting with a 3 mm / US 2.5 double-pointed needle.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
245 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 86 0 R
/E (Start by picking up and knitting sts as follows:      )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
246 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 86 0 R
/E (Pick up and knit 1 stitch for every stitch along the complete edge of the cardigan, starting at the bottom of the left side \(when looking at the cardigan from the front, RS facing you\), around the back neck, and down to the end of the right side with a 3 mm / US 2.5 80-100 cm or a longer needle \(or, you can also use two circular needles for this\). The amount of picked up sts will depend a bit on how long your cardigan is. Cut the yarn.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
247 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 86 0 R
/E (Place 5 removable stitch markers to mark where the bottom of the buttonholes will be worked along the left front edge of the cardigan \(when looking at the cardigan from the front, RS facing you\). Place the bottom buttonhole )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
248 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 86 0 R
/E (4 sts from the bottom edge of the hem, and place the top bottom of the buttonhole just at the point where the neckline shaping begins. Place the 3 other buttonholes evenly spaced out between the top and bottom buttonhole. Note! See the instructions on how to work the buttonholes below. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
249 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 86 0 R
/E (Join in new yarn and work the double knitted placket. Start from the bottom of the left side \(when looking at the cardigan from the front, RS facing you\) and following up and around the entire edge of the cardigan.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
250 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 86 0 R
/E (Work as follows:      )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
251 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 86 0 R
/E (Cast on 9 new sts on the 3 mm / US 2.5 circular needle in addition to the picked up sts on the left front edge of the cardigan using the Italian Cast-on method \(make the first and last st of the cast on sts purl sts\). )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
252 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 86 0 R
